WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:10.568
Mandy could not believe it.

2
00:00:10.569 --> 00:00:13.504
She was aboard the Santa Maria.

3
00:00:13.505 --> 00:00:16.837
And it was sailing away from the dock.

4
00:00:16.838 --> 00:00:20.599
"Where is Vinnie?" she wondered.

5
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.535
Diego had disappeared too.

6
00:00:23.536 --> 00:00:27.035
Then Mandy spotted a familiar figure.

7
00:00:27.036 --> 00:00:32.162
It was Christopher Columbus, and he was speaking with some sailors.

8
00:00:32.163 --> 00:00:36.297
"Excuse me, sir!" she called out.

9
00:00:36.298 --> 00:00:39.856
Mandy took the book out of her pocket.

10
00:00:39.857 --> 00:00:42.997
A sailor grabbed her arm.

11
00:00:42.998 --> 00:00:47.654
"How did you get on the ship?" he asked, surprised.

12
00:00:47.655 --> 00:00:50.485
"You're a little girl!"

13
00:00:50.486 --> 00:00:54.729
"Wait a minute!" Christopher Columbus interrupted.

14
00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:58.171
"What do you have in your hand?"

15
00:00:58.172 --> 00:01:02.865
"This is why I'm here, sir," explained Mandy.

16
00:01:02.866 --> 00:01:05.719
"I found your book in the church.

17
00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:09.094
I knew it was important to you."

18
00:01:09.095 --> 00:01:13.063
"I thought it was lost," Columbus said.

19
00:01:13.064 --> 00:01:15.970
"This must be a sign from God.

20
00:01:15.971 --> 00:01:19.055
You have brought good luck for our journey."

21
00:01:19.056 --> 00:01:24.222
On another part of the ship, Vinnie was looking around.

22
00:01:24.223 --> 00:01:30.999
After he helped gather the spilled potatoes, Vinnie had somehow lost Mandy.

23
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.107
The ship was full of activity.

24
00:01:34.108 --> 00:01:38.192
The Santa Maria was long and narrow.

25
00:01:38.193 --> 00:01:42.561
Vinnie counted more than 35 sailors aboard.

26
00:01:42.562 --> 00:01:49.319
They were uncoiling ropes, connecting equipment, and opening the large, white sails.

27
00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:53.981
Before he knew it, the ship was in open water.

28
00:01:53.982 --> 00:01:58.027
"I wonder what Mandy's doing," he thought.

29
00:01:58.028 --> 00:02:00.565
He looked behind him.

30
00:02:00.566 --> 00:02:04.642
The Niña and Pinta were following closely.

31
00:02:04.643 --> 00:02:08.794
They were smaller ships with fewer sailors.

32
00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:13.485
"Don't just stand there," said a young boy about Vinnie's age.

33
00:02:13.486 --> 00:02:16.173
He was holding a mop.

34
00:02:16.174 --> 00:02:20.399
"You'll get in trouble. Here, take this."

35
00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:24.084
"But, I'm not—," Vinnie began.

36
00:02:24.085 --> 00:02:27.234
The boy gave Vinnie an odd look.

37
00:02:27.235 --> 00:02:30.789
A big sailor walked over to them.

38
00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:35.035
"Why are you just standing there?" he demanded.

39
00:02:35.036 --> 00:02:37.552
"Get to work!"

40
00:02:37.553 --> 00:02:40.310
"Yes, sir!" cried Vinnie.

41
00:02:40.311 --> 00:02:43.694
He started mopping the deck quickly.

42
00:02:43.695 --> 00:02:46.309
The sailor walked away.

43
00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:50.651
"Thanks for the warning," Vinnie said to the boy.

44
00:02:50.652 --> 00:02:53.961
"I'm Manuel," the boy said.

45
00:02:53.962 --> 00:02:56.465
"This is my first time sailing.

46
00:02:56.466 --> 00:02:58.246
How about you?"

47
00:02:58.247 --> 00:03:01.818
"My first time too," said Vinnie.

48
00:03:01.819 --> 00:03:05.386
Together, the boys mopped the deck.

49
00:03:05.387 --> 00:03:09.054
It was wet from the mist of the ocean waves.

50
00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:16.023
Meanwhile, Mandy stood listening as Christopher Columbus spoke to some of his crew.

51
00:03:16.024 --> 00:03:20.885
She realized that each of them had a different job.

52
00:03:20.886 --> 00:03:23.600
One man was a carpenter.

53
00:03:23.601 --> 00:03:26.165
Another was a cook.

54
00:03:26.166 --> 00:03:30.582
A silversmith and a doctor were on board too.

55
00:03:30.583 --> 00:03:35.225
"Unexpected things happen at sea," Columbus was saying.

56
00:03:35.226 --> 00:03:39.899
"Each of you has a duty to make sure this voyage is successful."

57
00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:46.285
"Any wood that needs repair, the men can see me," said the carpenter.

58
00:03:46.286 --> 00:03:51.138
"I'll keep the meat well salted," said the cook.

59
00:03:51.139 --> 00:03:57.807
"Captain, I'll make sure your instruments are working perfectly," said the silversmith.

60
00:03:57.808 --> 00:04:04.847
"If any men get sick or break their bones, I will take care of them," said the doctor.

61
00:04:04.848 --> 00:04:11.371
"Good. And every day, I expect a report from each of you," said Columbus.

62
00:04:11.372 --> 00:04:22.372
"Yes, Captain," the men said.
